  ("see a true probability denoted p and its estimate denoted p^. In this book we are" 0.17856 0.85713 0.2376 0.26525 0.26387 0.02141 0.00473 0.2763 0.0254 "ELLVYP+MinionPro-Regular" 0.0159 nil nil 0 "ELLVYP+MinionPro-Regular" nil)
  ("almost always talking about estimates from data, and putting hats on everything" 0.17857 0.85714 0.26289 0.2843 0.2843 0.02141 0.00473 0.3190 0.0561 "ELLVYP+MinionPro-Regular" 0.0159 nil nil 0 "ELLVYP+MinionPro-Regular" nil)
